    {
      "id": "wneg1ui",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "GOVERNOR"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Governor acts as the constitutional executive head of the state and as a vital link between the Union and the State.",
        "Qualifications require the person to be a citizen of India and to have completed 35 years of age.",
        "The Governor holds office during the pleasure of the President, typically serving a term of five years.",
        "The powers of the Governor are broadly categorized into Executive, Legislative, Financial, Judicial, and Discretionary powers.",
        "Important Supreme Court cases have laid down guidelines regarding the imposition of President's Rule and the misuse of discretionary powers."
      ],
      "id": "pqnu5f8"
    },
