    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Governor holds office during the pleasure of the President and does not enjoy fixed security of tenure.",
        "Unlike the President, the Governor possesses explicit constitutional discretionary powers under Article 163.",
        "The Governor cannot grant pardon for a death sentence; that power lies exclusively with the President of India."
      ],
